# EtSelectionTileGroup Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtSelectionTileGroup` is a controlled tile-based selection group for the eToro design system. It renders a vertical list of large tappable tiles with configurable right-side elements. It provides:

- **Compound component pattern**: `EtSelectionTileGroup.Option` subcomponent
- **Four visual variants**: `icon` (default), `radio`, `toggle`, `toggleInput`
- **Two sizes**: `small` (default, content-driven height) and `large` (84px min height — use for prominent, standalone choices like KYC gender/personal-details)
- **Single and multi select**: single select for all variants, multi select for `toggle`/`toggleInput`
- **Customizable icon**: `iconName` prop on Option overrides the default chevron in `icon` variant
- **Subtitle support**: optional secondary text line on options (primarily for `radio` variant)
- **Border highlight**: selected state shown by visible border (for `icon` and `radio` variants)
- **Haptic feedback**: enabled by default

**Does NOT handle:**

- Form validation logic (handle in parent)
- Horizontal layout (always vertical)
- Error state styling (unlike EtRadioGroup)
- Labels or titles above the group (use external EtText)

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `EtSelectionTileGroup` (main component)

Uses a discriminated union for single vs multi select:

**Single select** (icon, radio, toggle, toggleInput with `selectionMode="single"`):

```tsx
<EtSelectionTileGroup
  variant?: 'icon' | 'radio' | 'toggle' | 'toggleInput' // default: 'icon'
  size?: 'small' | 'large'                // default: 'small'
  selectionMode?: 'single'                // default: 'single'
  value: string | null                    // required - currently selected value
  onChange: (value: string) => void       // required - selection callback
  disabled?: boolean                      // default: false
  haptics?: boolean                       // default: true
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
  accessibilityLabel?: string
>
  {children}
</EtSelectionTileGroup>
```

**Multi select** (toggle/toggleInput only):

```tsx
<EtSelectionTileGroup
  variant="toggle" | "toggleInput"        // required for multi
  selectionMode="multi"                   // required for multi
  size?: 'small' | 'large'                // default: 'small'
  value: string[]                         // required - currently selected values
  onChange: (value: string[]) => void     // required - selection callback
  disabled?: boolean
  haptics?: boolean
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
  accessibilityLabel?: string
>
  {children}
</EtSelectionTileGroup>
```

### `EtSelectionTileGroup.Option`

```tsx
<EtSelectionTileGroup.Option
  value: string                // required - unique value for this option
  subtitle?: string            // secondary text line
  iconName?: string            // icon name for 'icon' variant (default: 'angle-right')
  input?: SelectionTileOptionInputProps // optional inline EtInput customizations for toggleInput
  disabled?: boolean           // default: false - option-level disabled
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
  accessibilityLabel?: string
>
  {children}                   // string - label text
</EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
```

## Usage Patterns

### Icon variant (default) — with chevron

```tsx
const [selected, setSelected] = useState<string | null>(null);

<EtSelectionTileGroup value={selected} onChange={setSelected}>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="female">Female</EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="male">Male</EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="other">I go by something else</EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
</EtSelectionTileGroup>
```

### Icon variant — large size (KYC / prominent choices)

```tsx
<EtSelectionTileGroup variant="icon" size="large" value={selected} onChange={setSelected}>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="female">Female</EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="male">Male</EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="other">I go by something else</EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
</EtSelectionTileGroup>
```

### Icon variant — custom icon per option

```tsx
<EtSelectionTileGroup variant="icon" value={selected} onChange={setSelected}>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="done" iconName="check">Done</EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="next" iconName="arrow-right">Next Step</EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
</EtSelectionTileGroup>
```

### Radio variant — with subtitle

```tsx
<EtSelectionTileGroup variant="radio" value={selected} onChange={setSelected}>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="conservative" subtitle="Low tolerance for risk">
    Very conservative
  </EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="moderate" subtitle="Balance risk & growth">
    Moderate
  </EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="aggressive" subtitle="Maximum risk exposure">
    Aggressive
  </EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
</EtSelectionTileGroup>
```

### Toggle variant — single select

```tsx
<EtSelectionTileGroup variant="toggle" value={selected} onChange={setSelected}>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="notifications">Push notifications</EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="emails">Email updates</EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
</EtSelectionTileGroup>
```

### Toggle variant — multi select

```tsx
const [selected, setSelected] = useState<string[]>([]);

<EtSelectionTileGroup variant="toggle" selectionMode="multi" value={selected} onChange={setSelected}>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="director">
    A director or a 10% shareholder of a publicly traded corporation.
  </EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="brokerage">
    Employed by a brokerage firm or securities exchange.
  </EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
</EtSelectionTileGroup>
```

### ToggleInput variant — multi select with inline input

```tsx
const [selected, setSelected] = useState<string[]>([]);

<EtSelectionTileGroup variant="toggleInput" selectionMode="multi" value={selected} onChange={setSelected}>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option
    value="director"
    input={{
      label: 'Please enter stock ticker',
      fieldProps: { placeholder: 'AAPL' },
    }}
  >
    A director or a 10% shareholder of a publicly traded corporation.
  </EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="brokerage">
    Employed by a brokerage firm or securities exchange.
  </EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
</EtSelectionTileGroup>
```

### Group disabled

```tsx
<EtSelectionTileGroup value={selected} onChange={setSelected} disabled>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="opt1">Disabled option 1</EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="opt2">Disabled option 2</EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
</EtSelectionTileGroup>
```

## Anti-patterns

### Using Option outside of SelectionTileGroup

```tsx
// BAD — throws runtime error
<EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="opt1">Option 1</EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
```

**Fix:** Always wrap Options inside `<EtSelectionTileGroup>`.

### Using multi select with non-toggle variant

```tsx
// BAD — multi select only works with toggle variant
<EtSelectionTileGroup variant="radio" selectionMode="multi" value={[]} onChange={setSelected}>
```

**Fix:** Multi select requires `variant="toggle"` or `variant="toggleInput"`.

### Duplicate values

```tsx
// BAD — values must be unique
<EtSelectionTileGroup value={selected} onChange={setSelected}>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="same">Option A</EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="same">Option B</EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
</EtSelectionTileGroup>
```

**Fix:** Each option must have a unique value.

### Using iconName with non-icon variant

```tsx
// BAD — iconName is only used by icon variant, ignored by radio/toggle
<EtSelectionTileGroup variant="radio" value={selected} onChange={setSelected}>
  <EtSelectionTileGroup.Option value="opt1" iconName="check">Option</EtSelectionTileGroup.Option>
</EtSelectionTileGroup>
```

**Fix:** Only set `iconName` on options when using `variant="icon"`.

## Dependencies & Edges

### Internal Dependencies

- `SelectionTileGroupContext` — React context for sharing group state with options
- `SelectionTileGroupProvider` — Context provider (handles memoization)
- `RadioIndicator` — Reused from `radio-group/components/radio-indicator.tsx` for `radio` variant
- `EtToggleSwitch` — Reused from `toggle-switch/et-toggle-switch.tsx` for `toggle` and `toggleInput` variants
- `EtInput` — Reused from `input/input-v2/et-input.tsx` for `toggleInput` variant
- `EtIconV2` — Icon component for `icon` variant
- `EtText` — Text rendering for labels and subtitles
- `useEtoroTheme` — Provides theme colors for tile styling

### External Dependencies

- `expo-haptics` — Haptic feedback on selection
- `react-native` — `Pressable`, `View`, `StyleSheet`
- `react-native-reanimated` — Used indirectly via `RadioIndicator` animations
- `react-native-gesture-handler` — Used indirectly via `EtToggleSwitch`

### Design System Integration

- Tile background: `textPrimaryNeutral` at 5% opacity
- Selected border: `textPrimaryNeutral` (for `icon` and `radio` variants)
- Subtitle text: `textSecondaryNeutral`
- Icon color: `textSecondaryNeutral`
- Tile dimensions: `size="small"` → content-driven height, 12px border radius, 16px padding; `size="large"` → 84px min height (same radius/padding)
- Gap between tiles: X3 (12px)

## Patterns & Pitfalls

### Variant Behavior Summary

| Variant       | Right element              | Selection indicator      | Accessibility role |
| ------------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------ |
| `icon`        | Customizable icon          | Border highlight         | `radio`            |
| `radio`       | Radio circle               | Border + filled dot      | `radio`            |
| `toggle`      | Toggle switch              | Switch state             | `switch`           |
| `toggleInput` | Toggle switch + EtInput    | Switch + visible EtInput | `switch`           |

### Selection Behavior

**Icon and Radio variants (single select):**

| Action                  | Result              |
| ----------------------- | ------------------- |
| Tap unselected option   | Selects that option |
| Tap selected option     | Nothing happens     |
| Tap disabled option     | Nothing happens     |

**Toggle/toggleInput variants (single select):**

| Action                  | Result              |
| ----------------------- | ------------------- |
| Toggle unselected       | Selects that option |
| Toggle selected         | Calls onChange       |
| Toggle disabled         | Nothing happens     |

**Toggle/toggleInput variants (multi select):**

| Action                    | Result                         |
| ------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| Toggle off → on           | Adds value to array            |
| Toggle on → off           | Removes value from array       |
| Toggle disabled           | Nothing happens                |

### Context Architecture

The group uses context to share state with options:

- `SelectionTileGroupContext` — defines the context shape
- `SelectionTileGroupProvider` — wraps children and provides memoized context value
- Context provides: `value`, `onSelect`, `disabled`, `variant`, `selectionMode`
- Options read `variant` from context to determine which right-side element to render

**File structure:**

```text
selection-tile-group/
├── api/
│   ├── index.ts
│   └── types.ts
├── context/
│   ├── index.ts
│   ├── selection-tile-group-context.tsx
│   └── selection-tile-group-provider.tsx
├── subcomponents/
│   ├── index.ts
│   └── selection-tile-option.tsx
├── et-selection-tile-group.tsx
├── et-selection-tile-group.test.tsx
├── index.ts
└── AGENTS.mdc
```

### Accessibility

Built-in accessibility support:

- Group: `accessibilityRole="radiogroup"` for single select, `"group"` for multi select
- Options: `accessibilityRole="radio"` for icon/radio, `"switch"` for toggle/toggleInput
- `accessibilityState={{ selected, disabled }}`
- `accessibilityLabel` defaults to option's `children` text

